# The Quarry's door on orchid (issue #10): https://quarry.lan, one site block
# for orchid's Caddy. The Aviary's config (project-squirrel/Servers/
# Caddyfile-orchid, synced to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile) takes this file in with
# one line at its END, after the lan_tls snippet is defined, beside the
# Conservatory's:
#
#     import /home/todd/quarry/Servers/Caddyfile.quarry
#
# A merge here never reloads Caddy: a reverse-proxy config that deploys itself
# could take every web surface in the house down at once. After a merge that
# changes this file, `sudo bash ~/quarry/Servers/install-orchid.sh` reloads it
# (it checks the config first).
#
# lan_tls is the house snippet: the private root's certificate, HSTS, and
# compression at the choke point (page HTML and route JSON; photos pass
# through untouched). The name needs a Pi-hole Local DNS record on pearl,
# quarry.lan -> 192.168.1.148. 3020 is the web unit's port.

quarry, quarry.lan {
	import lan_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3020
}
